        // ------------------------------------------------------------------ Getting started
        new("Getting started", "How LegacyAVR works",
            "Windows and your games play into a virtual 7.1 sound card (VB-CABLE). LegacyAVR listens to that cable, turns the audio into Dolby Digital or DTS (the formats older AVRs, soundbars and TVs understand), and sends it to your real HDMI or optical output. Your AVR then decodes it just like a Blu-ray player's signal.",
            "Everything plays through the cable, so the cable must be the Windows default device. The HDMI/optical device is only used by LegacyAVR.",
            "Follow the Setup guide tab once, apply a profile, then run the Diagnostics wizard.",
            "overview beginner start vb-cable virtual cable"),

        // ------------------------------------------------------------------ Devices
        new("Devices", "Input device",
            "Where LegacyAVR takes audio from. Choose the virtual cable's playback side (\"CABLE Input\"). LegacyAVR captures it in loopback, i.e. it hears exactly what Windows plays into it.",
            "Choosing a recording device (e.g. \"CABLE Output\") also works but adds a little latency. Never choose the same device as the output: that would feed back, so the engine refuses it.",
            "CABLE Input, configured as 7.1 Surround at 48 kHz.",
            "loopback capture cable input source"),
        new("Devices", "Output device",
            "The physical output connected to your AVR or TV: HDMI (ARC) or optical/coax S/PDIF. The [DD] [DTS] [DD+] tags show which bitstream formats Windows says the device accepts, and the Format list marks formats the selected device did not advertise as unsupported.",
            "If a format is not tagged, the device (or the TV/AVR behind it) did not advertise it. Choosing it will make LegacyAVR fall back to PCM.",
            "Your HDMI or optical device that lists [DD]. Press Default next to it so it is chosen every time LegacyAVR starts.",
            "hdmi arc spdif optical toslink coax sink"),
        new("Devices", "Default output (the Default button)",
            "LegacyAVR's own default output. The Default button appears next to the output box only while the selected output is not already the default; press it and that output is selected every time LegacyAVR starts. The default is marked \"(Default)\" in the list. This never changes Windows' own default playback device (which should stay the virtual cable) - the Windows default is marked \"Windows default\" instead.",
            "If the saved output is not connected when LegacyAVR starts, the box shows it as \"(not connected)\" and a note explains it, instead of going blank or quietly picking another device. Reconnect it, or pick another output.",
            "Select your AVR / TV output and press Default once.",
            "default output device startup remember blank empty not connected hdmi"),

