        new("Encoder", "Output safety margin (latency)",
            "Extra audio kept queued in front of the HDMI/optical device, on top of what your devices need anyway. LegacyAVR measures that need: one capture packet from Windows (normally 10 ms) plus half an output period plus 2 ms. A margin below it is raised automatically, so every choice is safe.",
            "Automatic uses the lowest safe margin (about 14-17 ms) for the best lip-sync and game response. A larger margin only adds delay, but can hide dropouts on a busy PC. The 32 ms Dolby/DTS frame is part of every encoder and comes on top. The Output & Profiles tab shows the margin in use and the expected total.",
