        // ------------------------------------------------------------------ Stereo & upmix
        new("Stereo & upmix", "Stereo handling modes",
            "The Upmixing card (Upmixing & Bass tab; called \"Stereo sources\" before 1.4). It decides what happens when the source is only stereo (music, YouTube, most desktop audio) - real multichannel audio is never upmixed:\n• Keep stereo: stays 2 channels, encoded in your chosen format.\n• Dynamic 3.1: adds a centre speaker and subwoofer.\n• Dynamic 5.1: also adds surrounds.\n• Without a dedicated subwoofer these two are shown as Dynamic 3.0 / 5.0: no LFE channel is created.\n• Lossless PCM 2.0: sends stereo as uncompressed PCM, and switches back to your Dolby/DTS format automatically when a game or film plays real surround.",
            "Upmixing fills the room but is artificial. Lossless PCM keeps music perfect, but the AVR re-syncs (about 1 s of silence) whenever the source switches between stereo and surround. Real 5.1/7.1 sources are never upmixed. Changing mode keeps all your upmix slider values.",
