        new("Speakers & levels", "Dedicated subwoofer (active / inactive)",
            "The switch in the Bass & Subwoofer card. Its label shows the state and the layout currently being sent, e.g. \"Dedicated subwoofer active (5.1)\" or \"Dedicated subwoofer inactive (5.0)\". Active (default): you have a subwoofer and LegacyAVR sends 5.1 / 3.1 with an LFE channel. Inactive: no subwoofer - LegacyAVR never generates an LFE channel: the Dynamic upmixes become 3.0 / 5.0, 5.0 / 7.0 sources stay without one, and Dolby Digital / DD+ are sent as 3/0 or 3/2 with no LFE channel. An LFE the source already has is folded into the front left and right speakers (or discarded - see the LFE switch).\n\nWhat each format can carry: Dolby Digital and Dolby Digital Plus encode 2.0, 3.0, 3.1, 5.0 and 5.1. DTS (this encoder) has no 3.x layout, so a 3.0 / 3.1 upmix is sent inside a 5.0 / 5.1 stream with silent surrounds - the live indicator says so. 7.0 / 7.1 cannot be sent as 7 channels: LegacyAVR's processing bus and these encoders stop at 5.1, so 7.x sources are folded to 5.x (side and back speakers combined) and shown as \"7.1 \u2192 5.0 fold-down\". A 7.1 PCM device receives 5.x with a silent back pair.",
            "Changing it re-opens the output (short re-sync). The LFE slider on the Mixer becomes \"LFE \u2192 FL/FR\" and sets how much of the source's LFE is folded in. Set the AVR's subwoofer to \"None\"/\"No\" to match.",
            "Active if you have a subwoofer, otherwise inactive. Without one, the Dynamic upmix modes are shown as 3.0 / 5.0 and LFE crossover / level are greyed out.",
