        new("Custom EQ", "Custom EQ (per channel)",
            "An optional five-band EQ on every output channel (FL, FR, C, LFE, SL, SR): a low shelf, three bells and a high shelf. Open it with the EQ button of a mixer strip (or \"Edit EQ...\" in the Bass card). Each band has frequency (logarithmic slider), gain (-6 to +6 dB) and, for the bells, Q (0.5 to 4: low = wide, high = narrow). The LFE channel's bands are limited to 20 - 200 Hz. \"Custom EQ\" switches the whole EQ on or off; \"EQ on this channel\" bypasses one channel. Bypassing never loses the settings, and they are saved in profiles and kept across restarts.",
            "It works on all PCM audio - stereo kept as stereo, upmixed stereo and real 5.1 / 7.1 - after routing and upmixing; a pre-encoded Dolby / DTS bitstream passes through untouched. Test signals stay flat so calibration is not affected. While Custom EQ is on it replaces the Bass slider. Every change glides in over a fraction of a second, so adjusting it never clicks.",
