            "Estimated delay from Windows playing a sound to it leaving the HDMI/optical port, added up from measured stages: Windows mixer + loopback, capture queue, resampler, the 1536-sample Dolby/DTS frame (16 ms on average), the output queue, the encoder look-ahead (5 ms), and the WASAPI buffer + driver. Your AVR adds its own decoding delay on top (typically 20-60 ms).",
            "The frame and the Windows side are fixed; the output queue is the part you control with the safety margin. Before v1.2.0 the readout counted the frame and part of the output period twice (about 16-25 ms too high). Expect roughly 70-85 ms with the automatic margin.",
            "Automatic safety margin. Use the AVR's lip-sync setting if video looks early.",
            "latency delay lag lip sync stages breakdown"),
        new("Stats & diagnostics", "Live processing indicator",
            "Shows what the engine is actually doing with the current audio, measured on every block - not what the settings would suggest: \"Stereo \u2192 5.1 upmix\", \"Stereo \u2192 3.0 upmix\" (no subwoofer), \"5.0 \u2192 5.1 LFE generation\", \"7.1 \u2192 5.1 fold-down\", \"5.1 \u2192 5.0 (no LFE channel out) | LFE \u2192 front L/R\", \"No upmix (discrete 5.1)\", \"Stereo \u2192 lossless PCM 2.0\", \"Bitstream passthrough\". It also says when a 3.x upmix travels in a 5.x DTS stream (\"surrounds silent\") and when PCM 2.0 is a downmix.",
            "Channels more than 50 dB below the front speakers are treated as leakage, not surround, so a little residue does not stop the upmixer or Lossless PCM.",
            "",
            "processing indicator upmix active state live"),
        new("Stats & diagnostics", "Input frequency range",
            "Under the input meters: the lowest and highest frequency in what Windows is sending, averaged over the last ~7 seconds (bands within 50 dB of the strongest one).",
            "Useful to see whether a source really has deep bass or treble (e.g. a stream capped at 16 kHz), and what reaches the LFE crossover.",
            "",
            "frequency range spectrum bass treble hz analysis"),
        new("Stats & diagnostics", "Output visualiser",
            "Meters for the channels that actually leave LegacyAVR: 5.1 / 3.1 (5.0 / 3.0 without a subwoofer) for Dolby, 5.x for DTS, FL/FR for 2.0, the device's channels for PCM (silent slots are dimmed). Bit-exact passthrough shows no levels because the audio is not decoded.",
            "Compare with the input meters to see upmixing, fold-down and LFE generation at work.",
