        // ------------------------------------------------------------------ Profiles (v1.4.0)
        new("Profiles", "Profiles",
            "One list for every saved set-up (it replaces the presets and device profiles of older versions). A profile saved now stores everything: the output device, format, bitrate, output mode, safety margin, stereo handling and upmix sliders, subwoofer switch, LFE crossover / level / generation and its resume time, game mode and its LFE switch, bass, Night Mode, every speaker trim and mute, the master level and the whole custom EQ. Select one and Apply; \"Save as new profile\" stores the current settings for the selected output; \"Save (overwrite)\" updates the selected profile; Delete removes it. The five starting profiles (Dolby Digital 640, DTS, DD+, Lossless PCM music, Late night) only store format and processing, so they work on any output and leave your speakers and EQ alone.",
            "Applying sends only the settings that differ, so the output is re-opened (about a second of silence) only when the format, mode, margin, device or subwoofer switch actually changes. A profile made for another output asks whether to switch to that output or apply it to the current one. Profiles converted from older presets are marked \"partial\". Stored in %APPDATA%\\LegacyAVR\\profiles.json; the old presets.json and device-profiles.json are converted once and left untouched.",
            "Set everything up for one output, then \"Save as new profile\" with a name like \"Living room AVR\".",
