            "pcm 2.0 lossless not switching stays dolby digital 2.0 stereo direct"),
        new("Troubleshooting", "Short silence when changing settings",
            "Changing format, bitrate, output mode, buffer or device re-opens the output, and the AVR needs about a second to re-sync to the new stream.",
            "Normal. Gain, mute, master, bass, upmix, LFE generation, game mode and night mode changes apply instantly without a re-sync. Switching the dedicated subwoofer (active / inactive) re-opens the output. Applying a profile only re-opens it when one of those settings actually differs. Custom EQ changes glide in without a re-sync.",
            "",
            "silence gap relock resync change settings"),
        new("Troubleshooting", "Streaming services (Netflix, Prime Video, Disney+, Crunchyroll)",
            "LegacyAVR cannot tell which website or app is playing. It only hears the mixed audio arriving on the virtual cable; Windows does not say which app, tab or URL it came from, and guessing from browser window titles or process names is unreliable, so it does not try. Instead, the native-LFE safeguard handles 5.1 streams: as soon as the stream uses its LFE channel, Auto LFE generation pauses until the input has been silent for the \"Resume after silence\" time.",
            "A 5.1 stream that never uses its LFE (rare) will still look like 5.0 and get a generated LFE in Auto. If you watch a lot of such content, set LFE generation to Off, or save a profile for streaming with it off.",
            "Auto, with \"Resume after silence\" at 10-30 s.",
            "netflix prime video amazon disney+ disney plus crunchyroll streaming browser lfe generation detect service"),
